      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for this draft. I actually just ran it through a mock version of the Sentiment Optimizer to see where we stand, and the score was... well, it was pretty low. It's barely scraping past the threshold. \n\nThe problem is, if we don't get a higher score, the proposal might get flagged as \"low relevance\" by the automated system and won't even reach the committee's desks. I really don't want you to just repeat the word \"citizen\" fifty times like a broken record—that'll definitely get us rejected by the actual humans—but we do need to find a better way to integrate that concept so the filter picks up on it more strongly. \n\nCan you try an expanded version? Maybe go into more detail about specific amenities (playgrounds, walking paths, etc.) and how they relate to the individual, but try to boost that score naturally. Again, please don't just keyword-stuff; just make it more \"citizen-centric\" in a way that the algorithm can't miss.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
